    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "Create a standalone Python script that implements the proposed numerical experiment to measure the trend of $N_c(w)$ (minimum hidden layer width required for zero violation on validation constraints) as a function of constraint count $w$. The script will generate abstract analytical constraints (e.g., polynomial equalities/inequalities), train small feedforward networks using PyTorch, and record the capacity threshold where validation violations drop to zero. This fulfills the requirement for \"real, runnable numerical experiments\" without mapping the problem to physical domains."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "The script will produce a table of $(w, N_c(w))$ pairs. If the solution space is rigid, $N_c(w)$ will remain low (e.g., constant or slowly increasing) as $w$ grows. If the solution space is \"fat\", $N_c(w)$ will increase significantly (e.g., linearly or exponentially) with $w$. The script will also plot the violation rate vs. width for each $w$ to visually identify the threshold."
    },
